            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0653" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg581"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10044/174.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Turkish Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Turkish Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic">April 27,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to make
                    known to your excellency that, in compliance with the national will and in
                    accordance with the Fetwa rendered by the Sheik-islam, the National Assembly,
                    consisting of the Senate and Chamber of Deputies, in the presence of the members
                    of the cabinet, to-day unanimously proclaimed the fall of the Sultan Abdul Hamid
                    and the accession to the imperial throne of the lawful heir under the name of
                    his Imperial Majesty the Sultan Mohammed V.</p>
                <p>His Majesty solemnly swore by the constitution. The ministers, senators,
                    deputies, and high dignitaries were accorded the honor of deposing at the foot
                    of the imperial throne the expression of their devotion and fidelity.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Kiazim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
